  "music": "w4-castle-clatter",
  "authorNotes": "Solo. Wide, generous piers (900px each) and two short, familiar lever-door and button-door crossings, both signals wired directly with no relay, both switches latching or trivial-minMass so nothing here should feel like a test after 01-04. Everything is gettable on one relaxed pass: relic-w4-05-a sits right on the starting pier, relic-w4-05-b right on the middle pier, camera-w4-05 by spawn, and the snapshot (allSeatsInFrame + allAirborne) is easiest mid-arc on either swing. key-w4-05 sits on the middle pier as a themed collectible only — per lib/bums-rush/types.ts, the `key` prop carries only a `lockId` with no signal output, and `door` requires a `signal` unconditionally, so there is currently no schema path for a key to gate a door the way lever/button/signalRelay do; this is flagged the same way earlier levels flag schema gaps (not mine to fix here) rather than forced into an invalid wiring. No checkpoint: the whole level stays comfortably under the no-checkpoint cap, and a death just means a short, easy replay."
